## Residuals vs fitted {#sec-res_fitted .core}

[**Core**]{.core-text}

[↑ top](#)

When the explanatory variable is continuous, we do not have distinct groups in which to compare the spread of residuals. Instead, we often plot our fitted values against our residuals.

We can visualise this using the results of a linear regression we performed in Practical 4 (@sec-linear_regression), where we looked at the relationship between annual mean temperature and annual total precipitation.

First, let's recreate this linear model and re-draw our plot.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
site_metadata <- read_csv("data/site_metadata.csv")

lm_temp_prec <- lm(
  annual_total_prec ~ annual_mean_temp,
  data = site_metadata
)
print(summary(lm_temp_prec))
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```

